---
functor: 1
title: vbar
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`vbar` · fence · bars, a size or a determinant.

# Form

`(a + b).vbar` on a group, `x.vbar` on a symbol.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `(x).vbar` | $(x).vbar$ | fence around the group |
| `(v).vbar.x2` | $(v).vbar.x2$ | fence around the group |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Bars, a size or a determinant. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | A kind can take this fence from a rule: `set abs(fence: vbar)`. |
| Construction | Brackets around a group or a symbol. The brackets grow with the content. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- Works on a group, `(a + b).vbar`, or on a symbol, `x.vbar`. Write `x2` after it to double the fence. Write `left` or `right` after it to keep one side only. A style rule can give a kind its fence: `set mat(fence: vbar)`.

# From LaTeX

`\lvert x \rvert` becomes `(x).vbar` or `abs(x)`, `\lVert v \rVert` becomes `(v).vbar.x2` or `norm(v)`.

